      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/55/28",
      "text": [
        " «لاَ يَنْبَغِي أَنْ يُسْتَظَلَّ فِي اَلْمَحْمِلِ وَ اَلْفَرْقُ بَيْنَهُمَا أَنَّ اَلْمَرْأَةَ تَطْمَثُ فِي شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ فَتَقْضِي اَلصِّيَامَ وَ لاَ تَقْضِي اَلصَّلاَةَ» قَالَ صَدَقْتَ جُعِلْتُ فِدَاكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2674 - It was narrated from Al-Husayn ibn Muslim, who said:\nI asked Abu Ja'far the Second (as): \"What is the difference between a tent (fusṭāṭ) and the shade of a litter (maḥmil)?\"\nImam (as) said: \"One should not seek shade in the maḥmil. The difference between them is like the case of a woman who menstruates during Month of Ramadan; she makes up the fasts but does not make up the prayers.\"\nI replied: \"You have spoken the truth, may I be your ransom.\""
        ]
      }
    },
